{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Yesterday I was in Versailles and saw the splendors there, including the Grand and Petit Trianon. The latter two are furnished, but the Palace of Versailles is not, so one sees only the splendor of its doors, walls, ceilings, and wall paintings. The latter are mostly entirely new and mediocre. The gardens are too old-fashioned French: wide squares with clipped hedges, groves, separate side plantings of trees, fountains, statues, colonnades, and so on. The number of marble statues in the garden is 130. The orangery is admirable, and the oldest tree was planted in the year 1420. In contrast, the Trianons have English, charming layouts, though also with whimsical artificial rocks and Swiss-style cottages. The greatest fuss is made about the jumping of the water, which we did not see, only the multitude of Neptunes, Tritons, frogs, and so on."}}],"created":1795220840,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":198,"prompt_tokens":323,"total_tokens":521,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-XXP9NS9qRa6wgGEjldjcBCF9vvpykvVa","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":323,"prompt_ms":439.468,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.3605820433436533,"prompt_per_second":734.9795662027725,"predicted_n":198,"predicted_ms":4686.728,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.790497461928933,"predicted_per_second":42.03358931860351}}